 ('Mishnah Kelim 1:8', 'LAW', "within the wall lesser holies eaten; the Temple Mount bars zavim, zavot, menstruants and mothers; THE CHEL bars gentiles and the CORPSE-IMPURE; the women's court the tevul yom (no hatat); the Israelites' court the lacking-atonement (a hatat); the priests' court Israelites but for laying, slaying, waving. CELL corpse_tumah('camps') -> the corpse-impure barred at the chel. Credited."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 1:9', 'CONTEXT', "the porch-to-altar space, the Hekhal, the Holy of Holies — the vestments and priesthood engines' rows; credited (four ledgers)."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:1', 'LAW', "vessels of wood, leather, bone and glass — simple clean, receptacles unclean, broken clean; EARTHEN vessels and sodium-carbonate ones: contract and convey through their airspace, convey by the outside, not made impure through their backs, clean when broken. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the earthenware's airspace rule (Chullin 25a)."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:2', 'DISPUTE', "the smallest earthen vessels and standing fragments — the sizes by former capacity (R. Yishmael) / by the pot-classes (R. Akiva); R. Yochanan b. Zakkai's two logs. The row vessel_minimums."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:3', 'LAW', "not susceptible among earthen vessels: the rimless tray, the broken pan, the pierced roasting pan, gutters, the cover turned basket-lid, the swimmers' barrel, the bed, stool, table, ship, earthen lamp — no inner part, no impurity on the outside. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the insusceptible earthenware."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:4', 'DISPUTE', "the lantern with an oil receptacle susceptible; the potter's mould at the finishing; the merchants' funnel (a measure — R. Yehuda b. Beteira / the buyer smells — R. Akiva). The row vessel_minimums."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:5', 'LAW', "the covers of wine, oil and papyrus jars not susceptible unless adapted as receptacles; the pot's cover with a hole or point not, without them yes (the vegetables drained / the contents turned out). CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the covers."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:6', 'DISPUTE', "a damaged jar in the furnace by its completion; the sprinkler — R. Eliezer b. Zadok not susceptible, R. Yose susceptible (drops). The row vessel_minimums."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:7', 'LAW', "susceptible earthenware: the rimmed tray, the whole fire-pan, the tray of dishes (one defiled — not all unless a projecting rim); the spice-box and double ink-pot by their walls (R. Yochanan b. Nuri: the thickness divided). CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the compound vessels."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 2:8', 'DISPUTE', "a torch susceptible; the lamp's reservoir through its airspace; the tzartzur's comb — R. Eliezer not, the Sages susceptible. The row vessel_minimums."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:1', 'LAW', "a needle or ring in an oven's floor seen but not projecting — the dough touching them makes the oven unclean; in the plaster of a sealed oven by the oven's state; in a jar's stopper — at the sides unclean, opposite the mouth clean; sunk under a garlic-peel of plaster clean. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the lid's plaster (19:15's cord-bound cover)."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:2', 'LAW', "a sealed jar of clean liquid with a siphon in the corpse's tent — Beit Shammai: the jar and liquid clean, the siphon unclean; Beit Hillel: the siphon too clean, then retracted to Beit Shammai. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the siphon (the lid's reach)."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:3', 'LAW', "a sheretz under the oven's floor — clean (fell alive); a needle or ring beneath — clean (there before); in the wood ashes unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the presumptions."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:4', 'DISPUTE', "a sponge of unclean liquid dried outside fallen into the oven's airspace — unclean (the liquid will emerge); turnip and reed grass likewise (R. Shimon: clean). The row vessel_airspace."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:5', 'LAW', "potsherds of unclean liquid in a heated oven's airspace unclean; fresh olive peat likewise, old clean; known to emit even after three years unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the airspace's liquids."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:6', 'LAW', "peat or skins prepared in cleanness and trodden by the unclean — the emerging liquid clean; the spindle hook, the goad's point, the ring in a brick brought into the corpse's tent — unclean; moved by a zav unclean; into a clean oven's airspace they defile it; terumah touching them clean. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the sunk metals in the tent (19:14's 'everything in the tent')."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:7', 'DISPUTE', "netting over an oven as a sealed lid split between oven and colander — the split's measure by the ox-goad's tip that cannot / can enter (R. Yehuda reversed); a curved split not straightened. The row lid_split."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 9:8', 'DISPUTE', "a hole in the oven's eye — a burning spindle staff in and out (R. Yehuda: unlit); at the side unlit (R. Yehuda: lit); R. Shimon's middle and side; the jar's stopper by the oat stalk's second knot, the stone jars by the reed's; made for wine or other liquids; made by a person; other vessels — for food the olive falls out, for liquid lets liquid out, either the stricter; the sealed cover admits a liquid. The row lid_split (19:15's cover's integrity)."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:1', 'LAW', "THE VESSELS THAT PROTECT WITH A TIGHT COVER — of dung, stone, clay, earthenware, sodium carbonate, a fish's bones or skin, a sea animal's, and always-clean wooden vessels; at the mouth or the side, standing or leaning; inverted, everything beneath to the deep (R. Eliezer unclean); all protect everything, earthenware only foods, liquids and earthenware. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the protecting list (Sifrei 126's census; Onkelos' inserted 'of earthenware')."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:2', 'LAW', "HOW SEALED — lime, gypsum, pitch, wax, mud, excrement, crude or potter's clay, any plastering; not tin or lead (a cover, not tight); not swollen fig-cakes or juice-dough (lest unfit) but if done, it protects. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> tzamid patil's materials (19:15 'a cord-bound cover')."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:3', 'DISPUTE', "a loose stopper that does not fall out — R. Yehuda protects, the Sages not; the finger-hold sunk within with a sheretz — the jar unclean; in the jar, its food unclean. The row lid_split."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:4', 'LAW', "a ball or coil of reed grass over the jar's mouth plastered at the sides only — no protection unless above or below too; a cloth patch likewise; paper or leather bound with a cord plastered at the sides protects. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the cord and the plaster."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:5', 'DISPUTE', "the jar's outer layer peeled with the pitch intact; brine pots sealed with gypsum level with the brim — R. Yehuda no protection, the Sages protection. The row lid_split."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:6', 'LAW', "a hole stopped by wine lees protects; a vine shoot plastered at the sides; two shoots plastered between too; a board over an oven plastered at the sides; two boards between too unless pegged or jointed. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the stopped holes."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:7', 'LAW', "an old oven within a new one with netting over the new — if removing the old drops the netting all unclean, else clean; a new within an old with netting over the old and no handbreadth between — the new's contents clean. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the nested ovens."),
 ('Mishnah Kelim 10:8', 'LAW', "pans one within another with level rims and a sheretz in one — that pan alone; perforated to admit liquid with the sheretz in the uppermost, all; in the lowest, it alone; the lowest projecting above, both; dripping liquid the rule. CELL corpse_tumah('open_vessel') -> the nested pans."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:1', 'LAW', "SIX DEGREES OF WATERS — pools under forty seahs: an unclean man drank then a clean, unclean; drew in a clean vessel, unclean; a terumah loaf fell and he washed in it, unclean, else clean. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades') -> the six as DATA (19:17's living water the top)."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:2', 'LAW', "drawn in an unclean vessel then a clean man drank, unclean; drawn again in a clean vessel unclean; the loaf by the washing. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades')."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:3', 'DISPUTE', "unclean water fell in and a clean man drank, unclean; drawn in a clean vessel unclean; the loaf by the washing (R. Shimon: unclean either way). The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:4', 'LAW', "a corpse fell in or an unclean man walked in and a clean man drank — clean; pools, cisterns, ditches, caverns, stopped rain flows and mikvehs under forty: clean while it rains; after, near a city or road unclean, far clean until the majority pass. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades') -> the corpse in the pool clean."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:5', 'DISPUTE', "when they become clean — Beit Shammai: increased and overflowing; Beit Hillel: increased; R. Shimon: overflowing; valid for challah and the hands. The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:6', 'LAW', "the second degree — unstopped rain flows: the unclean drinker, the vessel and the loaf all clean; valid for terumah and the hands. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades')."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:7', 'LAW', "the third — a mikveh of forty seahs: persons and things immersed; the fourth — a small spring increased by drawn water: cleanses standing as a mikveh, immerses in any quantity as a spring. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades') -> forty seahs."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 1:8', 'LAW', "the fifth — smitten waters purify flowing; the sixth — LIVING WATERS: the zav's immersion, the leper's sprinkling, and THE HATAT WATER'S preparation. CELL corpse_tumah('living_water') -> the top degree (19:17; Lev 14:5; 15:13 — metzora and clocks by CALL)."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:1', 'LAW', "an unclean man who went down to immerse — a doubt whether he immersed, whether the mikveh held forty, which of two: unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades') -> the doubt unclean."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:2', 'DISPUTE', "a mikveh found lacking — all purified in it retroactively unclean, in private or public; a serious uncleanness; a lesser one (unclean foods, drawn water on the head) in doubt clean (R. Yose: unclean until known clean; a doubt of becoming unclean clean). The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:3', 'LAW', "a doubt about drawn water — whether three logs fell, whether forty were there, which of two: clean (a possibility to rely on); both under forty: unclean. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades') -> the drawn-water doubt."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:4', 'DISPUTE', "R. Eliezer: a quarter-log of drawn water at the beginning invalidates, three logs on the surface; the Sages: three logs beginning and end. The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:5', 'DISPUTE', "three cavities each with a log of drawn water — forty of valid water in before the third, valid; else invalid (R. Shimon valid — a mikveh adjoining a mikveh). The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:6', 'DISPUTE', "mud scraped to the sides and three logs drawn from it — valid; removed and three logs drawn into the mikveh, invalid (R. Shimon valid — no intention). The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:7', 'DISPUTE', "wine-jars on the roof filled with rain — R. Eliezer: broken in the rainy season with a little water in the cistern; R. Yehoshua: broken or tilted either way, not emptied. The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:8', 'DISPUTE', "the plasterer's lime-tub in the cistern filled — broken if water flowed above it (R. Eliezer) / either way (R. Yehoshua). The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:9', 'LAW', "wine-jars arranged in a cistern and filled — broken though the cistern's water was soaked up. CELL corpse_tumah('mikveh_grades')."),
 ('Mishnah Mikvaot 2:10', 'DISPUTE', "forty seahs of water and mud — immersed in the water not the mud (R. Eliezer) / in both (R. Yehoshua); the mud's definition by seven authorities (the reed, the rod, the plummet, the jar's mouth, the skin's tube, the log measure). The row mikveh_grades."),
 ('Mishnah Keritot 1:1', 'LAW', "THE THIRTY-SIX KARET CASES — among them ONE WHO ENTERS THE TEMPLE IMPURE and the impure who ate holies. CELL corpse_tumah('karet_entry') -> the entry on the list (19:13, 19:20 the punishment; sanctions' mode by CALL). Credited (twelve ledgers)."),
